    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0194" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 23700/14.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Beaupré.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to legation’s, April 11, relative to extradition of Knepper, Mr. Hale
                    says permission for transit has not been obtained and instructs Mr. Beaupré to
                    cooperate with the legation at Brussels to secure same, as agent is sailing on
                    this date.</p>
            </div>
